# art_library.b3t with a red sticker, to check the colour order of a target
# read back under --renderer=native (src/Render/bitmap_readback.h writes each
# texel as bytes A R G B), and under --renderer=emulated without a
# readback_resolve setting (band3 has the emulated GPU read the art maker
# back itself). art_library.b3t's sticker is grey, so red and blue
# swapped wouldn't show; this one is Paul Slifer's Red Hot & Blue Tattoo's
# first sticker (the wizard and the dragon), its colour changed to the
# palette's red (Change Color, the fifth swatch). Swapped, the saved piece
# would come out blue where the art maker's clipboard is red.
# From where render_screens_boot.b3t leaves Rock Band 3 Deluxe (the welcome
# hint, on a fresh profile):
#   python tools/band3ctl.py launch --fresh -- --renderer=native --test_random_seed=21 --async_shader_compilation=false
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/render_screens_boot.b3t
#   python tools/band3ctl.py run tests/game/art_library_color.b3t
# The reference is --renderer=emulated --readback_resolve=full, where the
# emulated GPU resolves the target into guest memory and the game's own
# untile reads it. Compare artc-library-new-closed's clipboard (the saved
# piece) between the two, and with artc-maker-layer (the target drawn live,
# right under either renderer).
# Screenshots are under screenshots/ next to the exe: artc-* the window's
# picture, artc-*-native the native renderer's drawing of the same moment.
# It leaves the game on the main menu.

# the welcome hint: Continue, to the main menu
wait screen=hint_rb3_welcome_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1s
press down
sleep 333ms
press green until screen=main_hub_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s

# Customize, Customize Band, Edit Band Logo: the Art Library, empty but for
# No Art
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 333ms
press down
sleep 500ms
press green
sleep 1s
press green until screen=manage_band_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1500ms
press down
sleep 500ms
press green until screen=patch_select_practice_space_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s

# Create New Art, the slot after No Art: the art maker (patch_screen)
press right
sleep 500ms
press green until screen=patch_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s
# Add New Layer's third category (Paul Slifer's Red Hot & Blue Tattoo) and
# its first sticker, black line art, which becomes Layer 1
press down
sleep 400ms
press down
sleep 400ms
press green
sleep 2s
press green
sleep 2s
# Layer 1's options (Move, Rotate, Scale, Change Color, ...): Change Color,
# whose swatches start white, grey, dark grey, black, red. Red turns the
# sticker's lines red; Confirm keeps it, Back returns to the layer menu
press green
sleep 1500ms
press down
sleep 400ms
press down
sleep 400ms
press down
sleep 400ms
press green
sleep 1500ms
press right
sleep 400ms
press right
sleep 400ms
press right
sleep 400ms
press right
sleep 1500ms
press green
sleep 1500ms
press red
sleep 2s
screenshot artc-maker-layer
screenshot native artc-maker-layer-native
# Finish Editing: the save prompt, with the old (blank) and new art
press red
sleep 2s
screenshot artc-maker-save
screenshot native artc-maker-save-native

# Save Changes: CopyToPatch runs, and the library comes back with the new
# piece chosen, its menu (Apply Art...) and the clipboard showing it
press green until screen=patch_select_screen timeout=30s
sleep 2s
screenshot artc-library-new
screenshot native artc-library-new-native
# back out of its menu: the library's thumbnail, the clipboard behind
press red
sleep 1500ms
screenshot artc-library-new-closed
screenshot native artc-library-new-closed-native

# back to the main menu
press red until screen=manage_band_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1500ms
press red until screen=main_hub_screen timeout=30s
sleep 1s
